From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:45:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] UefiPayloadPkg: The mapped store as runtime MMIO where the
 GCD has a hole

SmmStoreLibInitialize() marks the memory mapped store as runtime, for
the code that reads it at runtime: with the reclaim by the platform,
the variable driver walks the store there in a reclaim after
ExitBootServices(). It asked the GCD for the descriptor of the store and
added the range only if that failed. GetMemorySpaceDescriptor() does not
fail on a hole of the map: it returns EfiGcdMemoryTypeNonExistent, and
the capabilities and attributes then set on the hole never reach the
memory map. coreboot on Haswell does not report the flash as reserved
(on Cannon Lake it does, and the payload makes it MMIO), so on a
ThinkPad W541 the store was not in the runtime memory map, the pointer
to it was not converted, and the first reclaim at runtime read the
physical address: "[Firmware Bug]: Page fault caused by firmware at PA:
0xff910048", and Linux turned the EFI runtime services off until the
next boot.

Add the range as runtime MMIO when the GCD has it as non-existent, and
set the attribute. If that fails the store still works through SMM: say
so and go on.

And in the variable driver: when the store in the flash cannot be
converted at SetVirtualAddressMap(), no reclaim at runtime, by the
platform either. A full store then fails the write, as before the
platform's reclaim, where the read would fault.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../Variable/RuntimeDxe/VariableDxe.c         | 10 +++++-
 UefiPayloadPkg/Library/SmmStoreLib/SmmStore.c | 34 ++++++++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 39 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/MdeModulePkg/Universal/Variable/RuntimeDxe/VariableDxe.c b/MdeModulePkg/Universal/Variable/RuntimeDxe/VariableDxe.c
index 441e872e6..d06760321 100644
--- a/MdeModulePkg/Universal/Variable/RuntimeDxe/VariableDxe.c
+++ b/MdeModulePkg/Universal/Variable/RuntimeDxe/VariableDxe.c
@@ -292,7 +292,15 @@ VariableClassAddressChangeEvent (
   EfiConvertPointer (0x0, (VOID **)&mVariableModuleGlobal->PlatformLangCodes);
   EfiConvertPointer (0x0, (VOID **)&mVariableModuleGlobal->LangCodes);
   EfiConvertPointer (0x0, (VOID **)&mVariableModuleGlobal->PlatformLang);
-  EfiConvertPointer (0x0, (VOID **)&mVariableModuleGlobal->VariableGlobal.NonVolatileVariableBase);
+  if (EFI_ERROR (EfiConvertPointer (0x0, (VOID **)&mVariableModuleGlobal->VariableGlobal.NonVolatileVariableBase))) {
+    //
+    // The store in the flash is not in the runtime memory map: a reclaim
+    // reads it there (Reclaim() walks the store at this address), so none at
+    // runtime, by the platform either. A full store then fails the write, as
+    // without the platform's reclaim, where the read would fault.
+    //
+    mPlatformVariableReclaim = NULL;
+  }
   EfiConvertPointer (0x0, (VOID **)&mVariableModuleGlobal->VariableGlobal.VolatileVariableBase);
   EfiConvertPointer (0x0, (VOID **)&mVariableModuleGlobal->VariableGlobal.HobVariableBase);
   EfiConvertPointer (0x0, (VOID **)&mVariableModuleGlobal);
diff --git a/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/SmmStoreLib/SmmStore.c b/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/SmmStoreLib/SmmStore.c
index f80a21b0b..8573f56ec 100644
--- a/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/SmmStoreLib/SmmStore.c
+++ b/UefiPayloadPkg/Library/SmmStoreLib/SmmStore.c
@@ -839,15 +839,21 @@ SmmStoreLibInitialize (
   // Mark the memory mapped store as MMIO memory
   //
   Status = gDS->GetMemorySpaceDescriptor (mSmmStoreInfo->MmioAddress, &GcdDescriptor);
-  if (EFI_ERROR (Status)) {
+  if (EFI_ERROR (Status) || (GcdDescriptor.GcdMemoryType == EfiGcdMemoryTypeNonExistent)) {
     DEBUG ((
       DEBUG_INFO,
-      "%a: No memory space descriptor for com buffer found\n",
+      "%a: No memory space descriptor for the mapped store found\n",
       __func__
       ));
 
     //
-    // Add a new entry if not covered by existing mapping
+    // Add a new entry if not covered by existing mapping, and mark it as
+    // runtime. GetMemorySpaceDescriptor() succeeds on a hole of the map too,
+    // with EfiGcdMemoryTypeNonExistent: the capabilities and attributes set
+    // on a hole never reach the memory map of the OS, and what reads the
+    // store there at runtime (the variable driver, in a reclaim) then reads
+    // an address that is not mapped. Where coreboot does not report the
+    // flash as reserved (Haswell), the store is in such a hole.
     //
     Status = gDS->AddMemorySpace (
                     EfiGcdMemoryTypeMemoryMappedIo,
@@ -855,7 +861,27 @@ SmmStoreLibInitialize (
                     mSmmStoreInfo->NumBlocks * mSmmStoreInfo->BlockSize,
                     EFI_MEMORY_UC | EFI_MEMORY_RUNTIME
                     );
-    ASSERT_EFI_ERROR (Status);
+    if (!EFI_ERROR (Status)) {
+      Status = gDS->SetMemorySpaceAttributes (
+                      mSmmStoreInfo->MmioAddress,
+                      mSmmStoreInfo->NumBlocks * mSmmStoreInfo->BlockSize,
+                      EFI_MEMORY_RUNTIME
+                      );
+    }
+
+    if (EFI_ERROR (Status)) {
+      //
+      // The store works without, through SMM: only its runtime mapping is
+      // missing, and the variable driver does not reclaim at runtime then.
+      //
+      DEBUG ((
+        DEBUG_WARN,
+        "%a: mapped store at 0x%lx not runtime MMIO: %r\n",
+        __func__,
+        mSmmStoreInfo->MmioAddress,
+        Status
+        ));
+    }
   } else {
     Status = gDS->SetMemorySpaceCapabilities (
       mSmmStoreInfo->MmioAddress,
